
# Java E-Commerce Management System

## Project Overview

This is a simple Java-based E-Commerce Management System developed using **Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) concepts**.

The project manages customer details and product information. It provides customer registration, login, searching, updating and deleting operations. It also supports product management, including adding products, searching products based on different conditions, updating prices and deleting products.

## Technologies Used
- Java
- Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)
- ArrayList
- IntelliJ IDEA

## Project Modules

### 1. Customer Management
- Register new customers.
- Search customers by ID, name, email and phone number.
- Find customers based on city.
- Validate customer login using email and password.
- Update customer name.
- Delete customer details.

### 2. Product Catalog Management
- Add new products.
- Display all available products.
- Search products using product ID and name.
- Search products by name and price.
- Filter products within a specific price range.
- Search products by company.
- Search products using name, company and price.
- Update product prices.
- Delete products.

## OOP Concepts Used

| OOP Concept | Implementation |
|---|---|
| Encapsulation | Private data members in Customer and Product classes with getters and setters. |
| Classes and Objects | Customer, Product, CustomerService and ProductCatalog classes. |
| Constructors | Initialize customer and product objects. |
| Abstraction | CustomerService and ProductCatalog provide methods to perform operations without exposing internal list handling. |
| Collections | ArrayList is used to store customer and product objects. |

